-- Newsroom drafts for 2026-11-14 (Saturday). Loaded once into EDITORIAL_REVIEW; an editor approves before anything is published.
-- Facts restated in Boston Daily's own words with attribution. Every story carries its own photo; none was used in an earlier package or in the open 2026-11-09, 2026-11-10 and 2026-11-12 drafts (grepped content/ and seed/).
-- loc.gov and Wikimedia Commons were unreachable from the newsroom sandbox on this run. Photo URLs are Library of Congress URLs built from item IDs confirmed by search (Carol M. Highsmith, HABS and Prints and Photographs collections, no known restrictions). Editor: confirm each photo loads and matches its caption; the image check removes any that do not.
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO stories (id, slug, lane, type, section_slug, status, sensitive, headline, dek, body, byline, hero_image_url, hero_image_credit, hero_image_rights, source_system, source_ref, priority, is_lead_candidate, created_by, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bd-20261114-trump-xi-putin-summit', 'trump-xi-putin-trilateral-meeting-apec-shenzhen', 'newsroom', 'news_story', 'white-house', 'EDITORIAL_REVIEW', 0, 'Trump will meet Xi and Putin together in China, the first three-way meeting of the U.S., Chinese and Russian leaders', 'The White House announced on Friday, Nov. 13, that the meeting will be held on the sidelines of the APEC summit in Shenzhen, where leaders gather Wednesday, Nov. 18, and Thursday, Nov. 19. Nuclear arms and the Iran war are on Trump''s agenda; Ukraine is not.', 'President Donald Trump will hold a three-way meeting with Chinese President Xi Jinping and Russian President Vladimir Putin on the sidelines of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation summit in Shenzhen, China, the White House announced on the evening of Friday, Nov. 13. Senior U.S. officials told reporters it would be the first such meeting of the three countries'' leaders, ABC News reported.

## The schedule

APEC''s Economic Leaders'' Meeting runs Wednesday, Nov. 18, and Thursday, Nov. 19, with leaders from 21 member economies, according to Euronews. Trump is due to leave Washington on Monday, Nov. 16, for an ASEAN meeting in the Philippines before traveling to Shenzhen, where he is also scheduled to hold separate talks with Xi. Elon Musk will travel with Trump to China but will not attend the meeting with Xi and Putin, Euronews and Al Jazeera reported.

## What is on the table

A White House spokesperson said Trump will discuss reducing nuclear weapons. The New START treaty between the United States and Russia lapsed in February, leaving the two largest nuclear arsenals without limits for the first time in more than 50 years, Al Jazeera reported. Trump has said he wants a new arms deal that includes China. U.S. officials also expect the war with Iran to come up.

A senior U.S. official said Russia''s war in Ukraine will not be discussed, because Washington runs a separate negotiating track with Kyiv and Moscow that does not include China, Euronews reported.

## Low expectations

A senior administration official told Reuters the White House does not expect to reach any agreement, according to Al Jazeera. Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov called the meeting "extremely significant," and Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy has voiced concern that a Ukraine deal could be discussed without Kyiv. Moscow and Beijing had not commented on the meeting when it was announced, Euronews reported.', 'Boston Daily Staff', 'https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:pnp:highsm:04900:04918/full/pct:25/0/default.jpg', 'Aerial view of the White House and the Eisenhower Executive Office Building, Washington (file). Photo: Carol M. Highsmith / Library of Congress (highsm.04918), no known restrictions', 'public_domain', 'newsroom', 'content/2026-11-14.sql', 9, 1, 'newsroom-assistant', '2026-11-14T10:45:00.000Z', '2026-11-14T10:45:00.000Z');
